  "summary": "Pangenome, long-read and coalescent-network studies address gene copy number variation, with simulation benchmarking supporting orthology-based gene family analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is gene copy number variation, addressed through sequence-resolved genomes and model-based inference. A gene-based pangenome of 140 C. elegans strains shows that hyper-divergent regions are enriched for copy-number variable environmental response genes and identifies a novel anthelmintic resistance locus. PacBio HiFi sequencing gives near-complete de novo genomes of recently isolated Malian P. falciparum, with variation in telomere-associated architecture. A coalescent duplication network model infers copy number history from copy counts alone, applied to NB-ARC domain counts of NLR genes. OrthoSimulator offers empirically calibrated simulations with known orthology ground truth, relevant to benchmarking gene family analysis. The phylogeny-localization and ancient DNA relatedness preprints are methodologically distinct and do not address copy number directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
